    rdf:value "that.” When Bond had done so, the policeman said, “You just come up to the magistrate whenever you like.” Shortly before the Assize met, one of the town-councillors came to Bond and asked him if he knew any men who were “sound” on this land question, whom he could recommend to be  elected by ballot  on the Jury. Bond said he didn’t. “How would so-and-so and so-and-so do?” Very well Bond thought, and in due course they were  chosen by ballot . The same evening after dark they came to him, all the Jury, to ask him his views on the land and the fence. The result was that no “true bill” was found against him. A man who "^^xsd:string ;
